From 0904e73af00d51f836fb816bde435b6de7dd4604 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:02:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Tier 1 if-conversion: no per-row setup in each round (#1382)

sqlite3.c's --tier1 -c took 1.22% more user cycles at fab53452 than on
main b7a95eed (9700X, 11 runs each), with ir_if_convert_round at 1.09%
of the profile. Each round of a function with a branch wrote every row's
alias and sunk link and zeroed a 12-byte fresh entry per row. The maps
now store their value plus one, so zeroed storage means "itself" and
"none"; fresh and moved are sized by the blocks (a row per phi, a
region's arm rows per head). sqlite3.c's code is byte-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EgbxnhF8qrFw65jSZZBXme
Signed-off-by: David Gonzalez Martin <davidgmbb@gmail.com>
